WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:39.280
The Amazon River Delta, 16th Century

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.140
If we make it back home with these we'll be rich.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.850
We lost most of our companions, but
that means we'll get their share.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:51.810
Hope they aren't mad!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.940
We killed ‘em all; they won't get mad.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.590
One's still alive?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.270
W-What?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.110
A curse!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.380
That's the legend of the cursed blowgun.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.180
The poison used then was curare.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:12.890
Curare?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.270
I've heard that word somewhere.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.360
Sure you

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.360
You see it in mystery novels all the time.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:21.990
For instance?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.910
Carter Dickson's "The Red Widow
Murders” is famous, for one

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.410
Don't act like you knew it!

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.450
Why am I always the scapegoat?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:37.790
Curare is a deadly poison that's extracted from the South
American Menispermaceae, which is a type of Ivy.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.460
It also induces paralysis and is sometimes
used as a tranquilizer in surgery.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.970
But what's something as dangerous as that
 doing in Kazumi's elementary school?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.020
The assistant principle was doing anthropological
research in South America

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.100
when he received it and the cursed
 blowgun I told you about, I hear.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.020
But...

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.610
The curare's gone?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:12.540
I told you it was dangerous and to make sure
you secure it carefully, Iwabome-sensei

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.790
I did, sir.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.290
Are you sure you put it here?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.000
Yes!

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.050
And the blowgun's gone from the storage room.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:23.670
Kazuma-kun!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.430
No, I was just...

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.180
I got the wrong room.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.560
Go back to class now, run along!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.350
The poison, curare, and the cursed blowgun.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.520
Who would do that?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.480
Maybe a prank, right?

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.740
But one wrong step and

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.650
I thought so too.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.530
So let's get permission and investigate Kazuma's school.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:45.800
Listen guys, you won't make it to middle school if you
can't do an easy formula like this in your head.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.390
Yeah, when it's done I'll have you loan
me the same monitor, as usual.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.520
Mantetsu's looking at you!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.870
So, to divide this fraction you swap
the nominator and the denominator.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:21.790
After you showed him up at math the other
day, he doesn't mess with you anymore.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:24.840
See ya!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.590
Who are you?

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:34.850
Weirdo!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.140
Un cool.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.310
Jeez. What's that outfit?

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.440
It seems like he thinks he's perfectly disguised.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.320
Nobody sticks a ruler out
of their backpack any more.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:52.700
My, my...

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:57.700
Yeah?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.910
How cool!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.660
Kya! How awesome!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:02.870
"Kya"?

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.050
Who are those guys,

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.680
Not your family, right?

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:15.880
A tutor or something?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.180
Well...

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.520
Kazuma-kun, what's all this fuss?

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.940
T-Tachikawa-sensei...

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.480
What's wrong?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.280
Look at him blush.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.490
Do you think he's in love with her?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:41.010
What?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.120
Excuse me, Tachikawa-sensei.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.630
Ebe-sensei.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:52.340
What are you thinking coming
to school in such a short skirt?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.470
But this really isn't that short a skirt...

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.680
You're still new here; are you going to argue with me?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:00.890
Now now...

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.390
I rather like short skirts.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.850
That's Iwadome-sensei

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.580
He was the one who manged the curare.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.360
What do you mean, you like them?

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.070
Ebe-sensei, don't you think that
yours is actually a bit long?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.910
You seem likely to step on it along with a piano pedal.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:23.620
See?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.420
Don't say "see"?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:30.920
Are you okay?

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.470
Now then, let's go,

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.470
Tachikawa-sensei.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.600
I have to get ready for class.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.980
Was that sexual harassment, right there?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.110
He said he liked short skirts.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.240
What are you doing here anyway?

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.110
I'm sorry.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.240
We're with DDS.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.120
DDS?

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.700
That famous detective school that Kazuma-kun goes to?

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.920
Actually, we heard that a sample of curare had
vanished from your lab and came to investigate

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.140
This looks kinda like a haunted house.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.640
It's the Assistant Principles's hobby.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.680
Amazon and African ritual tools.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.020
The cursed blowgun was here, right?

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.070
Something's missing from here.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.450
Looks like a box was moved recently.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.780
What kind of box was it?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.660
Who knows?

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:45.950
Assistant Principal-sensei.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.750
Are you those "Day-Day-Ess"

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.370
Uh, we're DDS.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.960
Day-Day-Ess is how you say it, isn't it?

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.670
He's been overseas a bunch of times, hasn't he?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.840
" Day"?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.510
Maybe he just uses an interpreter?

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:06.560
Iwadome-sensei was acting like somebody
important had come, but it's just kids?

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.730
More importantly, we'd like to ask you
about the missing "cursed blowgun".

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.650
I don't know anything about that!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.690
Get out of here!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.360
He doesn't know anything? Yeah right.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:28.250
He'd probably get in trouble if people found out
that he was keeping curare at the school.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.790
But he'll be in even bigger trouble if something happens.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.500
Huh?

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.390
What's wrong?

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.180
I forgot my cell.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:37.720
Oh, it's in the Home Ec. room.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.300
Really!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.220
I'll go get it!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.600
Have fun.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.560
Why would I lie?

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.450
But Tachikawa-sensei's still there.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.530
The lights are still on.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.990
Let's go see her later!

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.340
What is this strange cold...

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:25.930
Atsushi, what happened?

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.800
Tachikawa-sense

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.480
Atsushi!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.020
Go get my friends at the gate.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:42.950
Sensei said that she'd bake us some cookies,
I were waiting.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.950
She was sitting in her chair, and then suddenly...

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.460
Sensei.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.040
Kazuma-kun!

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:58.790
It's fine!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.460
Calm down!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.590
What's wrong, Kazuma?

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.220
That scream just now.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.510
What's going on?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.310
Hurry and call an ambulance!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:12.560
Right?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.810
Just what happened?

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:19.650
Tachikawa-sensei was probably hit
with a dart covered in curare!

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.110
Curare?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:25.280
If the poison's curare then there's a possibility
her lungs will be paralyzed and she'll suffocate!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:39.080
If she was sitting in that chair then the dart came from...

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.180
A blowgun!

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.350
That was stolen from the storeroom, wasn't it?

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.270
Y-yeah.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.190
Dammit, who would do this to Tachikawa-sensei?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.110
The criminal should still be in the next room.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.530
Kyuu, hold that door.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:10.370
Got it.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.040
I'll head to the Home Ec. room.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.090
Kazuma-kun, you're going inside?

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.760
You can't be a detective if you're
« scared of the criminal, can you?

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.640
I'm am member of the DDS Q-class!

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.480
Kazuma-kun.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.900
The window's shut too.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.530
So does that mean they're in the kitchen over there?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.280
Well?

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.660
Nobody's there.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.660
The window's shut here too.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.670
Then where is he?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.210
There's nowhere for him to run.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.170
He vanished into thin air.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.460
That's impossible.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:11.470
But somebody shot her with that dart!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.350
Somebody did this!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.930
They can't just disappear!

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.350
Meg, how is she?

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.900
It seems like she'll be okay.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.440
It wasn't enough to paralyze her lungs.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.280
Sense!

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.110
Sensei, hang on!

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.400
Alright, let's go.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:51.690
Wait.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:53.070
What is it?

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.410
Take me to Takekawa Hospital.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.820
It's pretty far.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.120
Please.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.060
Understood.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.350
Hey, we're going to Takekawa.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.360
I wonder if she's okay.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:12.950
She is.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:18.080
But if there'd been any more curare on that
dart then she might've been in danger.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.910
Who would do that to her?

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.670
What a disaster.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.130
I never thought this would happen in our school.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.840
It's because you keep bringing
weird stuff here from overseas!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:42.480
That's not fair!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:48.440
Now that I think about it, I heard
the reason Tachikawa-sensei

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:52.410
Note Japanese have yea round schools

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:52.990
took vacation from the end of June until summer vacation
 was because you kept hanging around her!

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:56.350
Are you saying I'm stalking?

00:15:56.830 --> 00:16:00.230
And before she came it was Ebe-sensei wasn't it?

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:02.610
Ebe-sensei and I...

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:03.780
Well...

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:07.070
Then what about you?

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:10.450
You kept going to the Home Ec.
room every day after school

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.530
saying you were "doing your rounds”.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:19.170
Hey guys, don't you think that it'd be better
to call the cops instead of arguing?

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.460
Police?

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.050
This is an attempted murder!

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:28.880
You're just a kid, don't order us around.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.390
Get out of here!

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:35.100
But sir, they're DDS, anyway...

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.060
I'll call them.

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:38.140
Wait!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.140
The police...

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:44.020
Even if you try and hide it, the
hospital will call the police.

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:49.240
Anyway, we'll secure the crime scene until they get here.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.490
You and the other teachers stay here.

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:00.670
Check EVERYTHING!

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:07.670
There's got to be an air duct or a hole or something
leading out of one of these two rooms!

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:08.720
You sure?

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:11.260
I can't see anything like that.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:15.350
I don't see anything that people could pass through.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.020
Look more carefully!

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.390
Calm down, Kazuma!

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:26.150
I can't stay calm when Tachikawa-sensei was attacked!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.610
For now, let's review what we've got.

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:30.650
Yeah.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:44.380
The arrow hit Tachikawa-sensei right when
Home Ec. room, right?

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:45.500
Yeah,

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:49.630
So you heard the scream and went to the prep room.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:54.390
Then we and the teachers all rushed in.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:18:02.770
If the person who shot her was in the kitchen, then
escaping out the Home Ec. room is impossible.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.480
And of course, the same with the prep room.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.060
Yeah.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:09.030
So Kinta went to call 119.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:11.950
and I stood in front of the door.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:16.200
Ryuu and others went into the
Ec. room from this entrance

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:18.740
and went to the kitchen, but he wasn't there.

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:23.160
In other words, the criminal vanished from a sealed room.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.590
The only place he could've gotten
out from is the windows.

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.880
But they were all locked,

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:35.010
and what's more this is the 3rd floor and
there's nothing down there but concrete.

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.850
I don't think they could jump from this height

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:41.680
and there's no Veranda to hide on or anything.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.060
What's wrong with the ventilators?

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.650
That's a pretty big ventilator.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:55.700
Do classrooms normally have ventilators?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:19:02.830
This is a Home Ec. room. If the smells from cooking
got out it could disrupt the other classes.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:03.870
Oh, I see!

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.630
Kazuma, what room is above this?

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.590
Ebe-sensei's music room.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:13.340
And below is Iwadome-sensei's lab.

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:18.300
Hey!

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.780
Is there something suspicious about them?

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:38.490
A wiretap.

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.700
Was this what you were looking for?

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:44.410
Hey, where are you going?

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:49.630
Ryuu's gone off on his own to check something.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:53.840
That might be better than all of us going together.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.880
Then I'll take that, since it's suspicious.

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:01.100
This is suspicious too. A cursed blowgun
used in an attempted murder.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:07.350
The arrow was firmly wedged between
the door and the frame.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:13.190
If she didn't come directly in front of it, they would've...

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.690
They knew she would.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:21.410
She was hit around the shoulder area.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:25.120
Since there's a back on this chair, he
could almost be sure she'd sit there.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:29.330
But if she moved just a little bit it would fail.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.750
That's true, but...

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:33.150
I'll check that out.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:37.320
Don't move!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.320
What are you doing,

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:44.240
That's not it. Just don't move, okay?

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.130
Is it a piece of garlic or something?

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.800
No, it might be a bit of cookie dough.

00:20:56.570 --> 00:21:00.050
Cookies were being baked in the
microwave when it happened.

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:04.510
No, that's just flour.

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:10.810
Anyway, I'll follow up on the cursed blowgun.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:15.070
I'm worried about how it just
vanished from the store room.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.610
You don't think somebody put a curse on her.

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:32.330
No way.

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:38.840
I'm Odajima, from the police station.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:44.760
DDS would be extremely helpful in our investigations.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.470
ls Day-Day-Ess that great?

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.100
They're just kids.

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:52.190
Actually, I thought the same thing.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.190
I was surprised later, though.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:29.390
Smoke?

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:39.480
It really is an impossible crime.

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:41.570
A curse, huh?

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.280
Something that unscientific is impossible!

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:51.830
If that dart flew then somebody must've blown

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:54.040
They can't disappear!

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:01.880
I won't forgive you for making Tachikawa-suffer.

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:03.720
I'll catch you!

00:23:05.370 --> 00:23:07.050
The smoke came from over here!

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:10.600
Kyuu, what is this?

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:24.620
Next time on Detective Academy Q

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:24.620
The Vanished Curse

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:22.820
Did you find something?

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:31.200
What are my mask and blowgun doing here?

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:08.980
Ryuu's so lucky...

00:25:09.380 --> 00:25:10.230
How so?

00:25:11.070 --> 00:25:14.450
All the kids go "Kya!" when they see him
 and all the women go "Kya!" when the see him?

00:25:14.710 --> 00:25:17.530
You've got better luck with guys, don't ya Kinta?

00:25:17.090 --> 00:25:18.990
You think? Oh, I'm blushing.

00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:21.710
THAT'S NOT WHAT I WANT!
